    fix(master-doc): select on the marker a fill actually writes, so the program converges (CF-257)
    
    The selector tested for `FILLED — ` only, but every module filled before the
    accepted-output writer changed carries `**VERIFIED — …**` as its Status row.
    Measured on this tree: 37 of the 45 docs/master modules already record a
    FILLED/VERIFIED completion. 31 of those are skipped anyway for having no
    `| Path |` field, but the 6 that carry one were re-selected on every run — each
    run re-filled documents it had already completed, so the program could never
    converge and `--force` meant nothing.
    
    is_complete() now reads the completions the writers actually emit —
    `**FILLED — `, `**VERIFIED — `, and the bare `**VERIFIED**` form one module
    uses — and main() calls it in place of the inline prefix test. `--force` still
    re-fills everything on purpose. Index exclusion and the `| Path |` guard are
    unchanged, and nothing a fill WRITES is touched.
    
    Measured: `python3 scripts/master_doc_fill.py --dry-run` printed
    `todo=11 provider=deepseek workers=2` with 6 verified modules among the
    candidates, and prints `todo=5` after the fix — the 5 whose Status is still
    RED/FAILING (38, 40-43). Section 52 gains two CF_MASTER_DIR fixtures: one with
    `| Status | **VERIFIED — …** |` and one with `| Status | **VERIFIED** |`, both
    keeping the template's RED string in their bodies exactly as a real fill leaves
    it. Neither may be a candidate, and `--force` still selects them. Against the
    pre-fix scripts/master_doc_fill.py those arms red with named rows (marker leak
    plus both convergence runs, 4 FAIL rows). No provider call and no real document
    was written; `bash docs/audits/cf198-section-mapping.sh` still prints
    arms_plan=55 arms_tree=55.
    
